# Master assets are immutable

Never modify original/master source files. Leave the master untouched. Always copy first and make all changes only to the copy.

## Canonical master location (in-repo)

Copy masters into the top-level **`masters/`** folder, mirroring character/asset identity:

- `masters/dorothy/Sprites/NEW/` — original sprite exports
- `masters/dorothy/meshes/` — master meshes/rigs
- `masters/<character>/…` — other originals

When new originals arrive (exports, downloads, TM restores), place or copy them under `masters/` first. Do not invent a second “master” tree under `models/` unless it is only a working mirror that stays read-only.

## Also treat as masters (do not write/delete/overwrite)

- Existing `models/**/NEW/`, `models/**/MASTER/`, `models/**/Original/` until migrated into `masters/`
- Any path the user labels as master/original/source-of-truth

## Copies / derived only

- Game/runtime packs under `models/` (e.g. `Sprites/game/`)
- Baked/retargeted GLBs, atlases, presentation JSON
- Working forks and pipeline outputs

Pipelines must **read from `masters/`** (or another labeled master) and **write only to a separate destination**. Never optimize, rename, or “fix” in place inside a master tree.
